  "question": "The project involves developing a data management system for the Consumer Expenditure Survey (CE) that facilitates the collection and analysis of data related to expenditures, income, and demographics in the United States. The system should handle public-use microdata files with appropriate privacy measures to avoid identifying individual respondents.\n\n1) Background / Context  \nThe Consumer Expenditure Survey (CE) is a national survey that gathers data on consumer spending, income, and demographics. This data is crucial for understanding consumer behavior and economic trends.\n\n2) Objectives  \nThe objective is to design and implement a system capable of storing and managing survey data for public use while preserving respondent anonymity. The system should support complex data analysis and reporting on consumer expenditure patterns.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users  \n- Stakeholders: Government agencies, economic researchers, policy makers.\n- Users: Data analysts, economists, statisticians, and researchers interested in consumer expenditure patterns.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions  \n- The system should collect and store data on household expenditures, incomes, and demographics efficiently.\n- Provide functionalities to query and analyze data by various demographic and economic factors.\n- Ensure data integrity and establish relationships between datasets such as expenditures and household information.\n- Allow users to download anonymized datasets for external analysis.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions  \n- The system must ensure data privacy by using anonymization techniques.\n- It should be scalable to handle large volumes of data across multiple years effectively.\n- The database operations should maintain high performance and fast query response times.\n- The system must adhere to strict compliance standards for handling sensitive public data.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0100\nCREATE TABLE `survey_year` (\n  `survey_year_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `release_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`survey_year_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_survey_year_year` (`year`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `household` (\n  `household_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `survey_year_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `anonymized_household_code` char(12) NOT NULL,\n  `region` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `urban_rural_status` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `household_size` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `num_children` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `home_ownership_status` varchar(30) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reference_person_age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reference_person_sex` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reference_person_race` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `education_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`household_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_household_anonymized_household_code` (`anonymized_household_code`),\n  KEY `household_ibfk_1` (`survey_year_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `household_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`survey_year_id`) REFERENCES `survey_year` (`survey_year_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `household_income` (\n  `household_income_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `household_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `income_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(12,2) NOT NULL,\n  `period` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`household_income_id`),\n  KEY `household_income_ibfk_1` (`household_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `household_income_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`household_id`) REFERENCES `household` (`household_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `expenditure_category` (\n  `expenditure_category_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `category_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_category_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`expenditure_category_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_expenditure_category_category_name` (`category_name`),\n  KEY `expenditure_category_ibfk_1` (`parent_category_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `expenditure_category_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_category_id`) REFERENCES `expenditure_category` (`expenditure_category_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `household_expenditure` (\n  `household_expenditure_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `household_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `expenditure_category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(12,2) NOT NULL,\n  `frequency` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reporting_period` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`household_expenditure_id`),\n  KEY `household_expenditure_ibfk_1` (`household_id`),\n  KEY `household_expenditure_ibfk_2` (`expenditure_category_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `household_expenditure_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`household_id`) REFERENCES `household` (`household_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `household_expenditure_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`expenditure_category_id`) REFERENCES `expenditure_category` (`expenditure_category_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dataset_download` (\n  `dataset_download_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `survey_year_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `file_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `file_format` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `anonymization_method` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `download_url` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`dataset_download_id`),\n  KEY `dataset_download_ibfk_1` (`survey_year_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `dataset_download_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`survey_year_id`) REFERENCES `survey_year` (`survey_year_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
